        <OtherAbstract Type="AIDS" Language="eng">
            <AbstractText>A European study looked for a correlation between consuming low doses of fish oil, a type of omega-3 fatty acid, and reduced incidences of coronary atherosclerosis. Much is still unknown about the medical benefit of omega-3 fatty acid. Although this was not an AIDS study, fish oil may or may not be appropriate in treating some HIV-infected patients with lipid abnormalities due to antiretroviral use.</AbstractText>
        </OtherAbstract>
